            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery fistula following rupture of aneurysm of the sinus node artery into the right atrium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of coronary artery fistula secondary to rupture of a coronary artery aneurysm is reported. The association of these 2 conditions is rare. Successful surgical treatment was achieved by use of a Dacron patch to close the fistula.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
